mod_audio_fork: ignore playAudio messages without a string audioContentType.

A playAudio text message from the WebSocket peer whose data object lacks a string audioContentType
reached strcmp(NULL) on the libwebsockets service thread and crashed FreeSWITCH. Such messages are
now logged at ERROR and ignored: no temp file, no playout entry, no play_audio event. Messages that
carry a string audioContentType, and messages without data, follow the original path unchanged.

Against drachtio-freeswitch-modules 88e1465908a89bed5c95d336aa53a3899bb5abb5, modules/mod_audio_fork.
Apply from the module directory: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0 --batch
--- a/lws_glue.cpp
+++ b/lws_glue.cpp
@@ -39,7 +39,10 @@
       switch_log_printf(SWITCH_CHANNEL_LOG, SWITCH_LOG_DEBUG, "(%u) processIncomingMessage - received %s message\n", tech_pvt->id, type.c_str());
       cJSON* jsonData = cJSON_GetObjectItem(json, "data");
       if (0 == type.compare("playAudio")) {
-        if (jsonData) {
+        if (jsonData && NULL == cJSON_GetObjectCstr(jsonData, "audioContentType")) {
+          switch_log_printf(SWITCH_CHANNEL_LOG, SWITCH_LOG_ERROR, "(%u) processIncomingMessage - playAudio request has no string audioContentType, ignoring\n", tech_pvt->id);
+        }
+        else if (jsonData) {
           // dont send actual audio bytes in event message
           cJSON* jsonFile = NULL;
           cJSON* jsonAudio = cJSON_DetachItemFromObject(jsonData, "audioContent");
